{"name":"Inness Sage","hex":"#959272","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"inness","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The quality of being in, or inside."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inness"},{"term":"sage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Wise.","Grave; serious; solemn."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very wise person or spiritual teacher; someone of gravity and wisdom, especially, a teacher venerable for years, and of sound judgment and prudence; a grave or stoic philosopher."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sage (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Sage is a grey-green resembling that of dried sage leaves. As a quaternary color, it is an equal mix of the tertiary colors citron and slate. The hex RGB color value of the adjacent sage swatch is BCB88A. For decades, some military flight jackets were made in sage green."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Sage_iPhone_17.jpg/330px-Sage_iPhone_17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sage_(color)","wikidata":"Q7399114"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"sage":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/79/En-us-sage.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/79/En-us-sage.ogg/En-us-sage.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Saint-Denis (93), basilique, gisant de Charles V sculpté lorsqu'il avait 27 ans 2","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Saint-Denis_%2893%29%2C_basilique%2C_gisant_de_Charles_V_sculpt%C3%A9_lorsqu%27il_avait_27_ans_2.jpg/500px-Saint-Denis_%2893%29%2C_basilique%2C_gisant_de_Charles_V_sculpt%C3%A9_lorsqu%27il_avait_27_ans_2.jpg","ratio":0.75,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint-Denis_(93),